#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:1
msgid "Name"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:3
msgid "`nix-store --query` - display information about store paths"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:5
msgid "Synopsis"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:7
msgid ""
"`nix-store` {`--query` | `-q`} {`--outputs` | `--requisites` | `-R` | `--"
"references` | `--referrers` | `--referrers-closure` | `--deriver` | `-d` | "
"`--valid-derivers` | `--graph` | `--tree` | `--binding` _name_ | `-b` _name_ "
"| `--hash` | `--size` | `--roots`} \\[`--use-output`\\] \\[`-u`\\] \\[`--"
"force-realise`\\] \\[`-f`\\] _paths…_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:15
msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:17
msgid ""
"The operation `--query` displays various bits of information about the store "
"paths . The queries are described below. At most one query can be specified. "
"The default query is `--outputs`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:21
msgid ""
"The paths _paths_ may also be symlinks from outside of the Nix store, to the "
"Nix store. In that case, the query is applied to the target of the symlink."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:25
msgid "Common query options"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:27
msgid "`--use-output` / `-u`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:29
msgid ""
"For each argument to the query that is a [store derivation](../../glossary."
"md#gloss-store-derivation), apply the query to the output path of the "
"derivation instead."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:32
msgid "`--force-realise` / `-f`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:34
msgid ""
"Realise each argument to the query first (see [`nix-store --realise`](./"
"realise.md))."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:38
msgid "Queries"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:40
msgid "`--outputs`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:42
msgid ""
"Prints out the [output paths](../../glossary.md#gloss-output-path) of the "
"store derivations _paths_. These are the paths that will be produced when "
"the derivation is built."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:48
msgid "`--references`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:50
msgid ""
"Prints the set of [references](../../glossary.md#gloss-reference) of the "
"store paths _paths_, that is, their immediate dependencies. (For _all_ "
"dependencies, use `--requisites`.)"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:56
msgid "`--requisites` / `-R`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:58
msgid ""
"Prints out the set of [_requisites_](../../glossary.md#gloss-requisite) "
"(better known as the [closure](../../glossary.md#gloss-closure)) of the "
"store path _paths_."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:63
msgid "This query has one option:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:65
msgid ""
"`--include-outputs` Also include the existing output paths of [store "
"derivation](../../glossary.md#gloss-store-derivation)s, and their closures."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:69
msgid ""
"This query can be used to implement various kinds of deployment. A _source "
"deployment_ is obtained by distributing the closure of a store derivation. A "
"_binary deployment_ is obtained by distributing the closure of an output "
"path. A _cache deployment_ (combined source/binary deployment, including "
"binaries of build-time-only dependencies) is obtained by distributing the "
"closure of a store derivation and specifying the option `--include-outputs`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:77
msgid "`--referrers`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:79
msgid ""
"Prints the set of [_referrers_](../../glossary.md#gloss-referrer) of the "
"store paths _paths_, that is, the store paths currently existing in the Nix "
"store that refer to one of _paths_. Note that contrary to the references, "
"the set of referrers is not constant; it can change as store paths are added "
"or removed."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:87
msgid "`--referrers-closure`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:89
msgid ""
"Prints the closure of the set of store paths _paths_ under the [referrers "
"relation](../../glossary.md#gloss-referrer); that is, all store paths that "
"directly or indirectly refer to one of _paths_. These are all the path "
"currently in the Nix store that are dependent on _paths_."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:96
msgid "`--deriver` / `-d`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:98
msgid ""
"Prints the [deriver](../../glossary.md#gloss-deriver) that was used to build "
"the store paths _paths_. If the path has no deriver (e.g., if it is a source "
"file), or if the deriver is not known (e.g., in the case of a binary-only "
"deployment), the string `unknown-deriver` is printed. The returned deriver "
"is not guaranteed to exist in the local store, for example when _paths_ were "
"substituted from a binary cache. Use `--valid-derivers` instead to obtain "
"valid paths only."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:108
msgid "`--valid-derivers`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:110
msgid ""
"Prints a set of derivation files (`.drv`) which are supposed produce said "
"paths when realized. Might print nothing, for example for source paths or "
"paths substituted from a binary cache."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:114
msgid "`--graph`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:116
msgid ""
"Prints the references graph of the store paths _paths_ in the format of the "
"`dot` tool of AT&T's [Graphviz package](http://www.graphviz.org/). This can "
"be used to visualise dependency graphs. To obtain a build-time dependency "
"graph, apply this to a store derivation. To obtain a runtime dependency "
"graph, apply it to an output path."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:123
msgid "`--tree`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:125
msgid ""
"Prints the references graph of the store paths _paths_ as a nested ASCII "
"tree. References are ordered by descending closure size; this tends to "
"flatten the tree, making it more readable. The query only recurses into a "
"store path when it is first encountered; this prevents a blowup of the tree "
"representation of the graph."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:131
msgid "`--graphml`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:133
msgid ""
"Prints the references graph of the store paths _paths_ in the [GraphML]"
"(http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/) file format. This can be used to "
"visualise dependency graphs. To obtain a build-time dependency graph, apply "
"this to a [store derivation](../../glossary.md#gloss-store-derivation). To "
"obtain a runtime dependency graph, apply it to an output path."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:139
msgid "`--binding` _name_ / `-b` _name_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:141
msgid ""
"Prints the value of the attribute _name_ (i.e., environment variable) of the "
"[store derivation](../../glossary.md#gloss-store-derivation)s _paths_. It is "
"an error for a derivation to not have the specified attribute."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:145
msgid "`--hash`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:147
msgid ""
"Prints the SHA-256 hash of the contents of the store paths _paths_ (that is, "
"the hash of the output of `nix-store --dump` on the given paths). Since the "
"hash is stored in the Nix database, this is a fast operation."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:152
msgid "`--size`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:154
msgid ""
"Prints the size in bytes of the contents of the store paths _paths_ — to be "
"precise, the size of the output of `nix-store --dump` on the given paths. "
"Note that the actual disk space required by the store paths may be higher, "
"especially on filesystems with large cluster sizes."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:160
msgid "`--roots`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:162
msgid ""
"Prints the garbage collector roots that point, directly or indirectly, at "
"the store paths _paths_."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:165
msgid "Options"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:167
msgid ""
"The following options are allowed for all `nix-store` operations, but may "
"not always have an effect."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:169
msgid "<span id=\"opt-add-root\">[`--add-root`](#opt-add-root)</span> _path_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:171
msgid ""
"Causes the result of a realisation (`--realise` and `--force-realise`) to be "
"registered as a root of the garbage collector. _path_ will be created as a "
"symlink to the resulting store path. In addition, a uniquely named symlink "
"to _path_ will be created in `/nix/var/nix/gcroots/auto/`. For instance,"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:187
msgid ""
"Thus, when `/home/eelco/bla/result` is removed, the GC root in the `auto` "
"directory becomes a dangling symlink and will be ignored by the collector."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:191
#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:276
msgid "**Warning**"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:193
msgid ""
"Note that it is not possible to move or rename GC roots, since the symlink "
"in the `auto` directory will still point to the old location."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:197
msgid ""
"If there are multiple results, then multiple symlinks will be created by "
"sequentially numbering symlinks beyond the first one (e.g., `foo`, `foo-2`, "
"`foo-3`, and so on)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:207
msgid "Common Options"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:209
msgid "Most Nix commands accept the following command-line options:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:211
msgid "<span id=\"opt-help\">[`--help`](#opt-help)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:213
msgid "Prints out a summary of the command syntax and exits."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:215
msgid "<span id=\"opt-version\">[`--version`](#opt-version)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:217
msgid "Prints out the Nix version number on standard output and exits."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:219
msgid ""
"For machine-readable output, including versions of the libraries Nix links "
"against, see the [`nix version`](../../command-ref/new-cli/nix3-version.md) "
"command."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:222
msgid "<span id=\"opt-verbose\">[`--verbose`](#opt-verbose)</span> / `-v`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:224
msgid ""
"Increases the level of verbosity of diagnostic messages printed on standard "
"error. For each Nix operation, the information printed on standard output is "
"well-defined; any diagnostic information is printed on standard error, never "
"on standard output."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:228
msgid ""
"This option may be specified repeatedly. Currently, the following verbosity "
"levels exist:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:231
msgid "`0` “Errors only”"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:233
msgid "Only print messages explaining why the Nix invocation failed."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:235
msgid "`1` “Informational”"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:237
msgid "Print _useful_ messages about what Nix is doing. This is the default."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:240
msgid "`2` “Talkative”"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:242
msgid "Print more informational messages."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:244
msgid "`3` “Chatty”"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:246
msgid "Print even more informational messages."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:248
msgid "`4` “Debug”"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:250
msgid "Print debug information."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:252
msgid "`5` “Vomit”"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:254
msgid "Print vast amounts of debug information."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:256
msgid "<span id=\"opt-quiet\">[`--quiet`](#opt-quiet)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:258
msgid ""
"Decreases the level of verbosity of diagnostic messages printed on standard "
"error. This is the inverse option to `-v` / `--verbose`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:261
msgid ""
"This option may be specified repeatedly. See the previous verbosity levels "
"list."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:264
msgid ""
"<span id=\"opt-log-format\">[`--log-format`](#opt-log-format)</span> _format_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:266
msgid ""
"This option can be used to change the output of the log format, with "
"_format_ being one of:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:268
msgid "`raw`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:270
msgid "This is the raw format, as outputted by nix-build."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:272
msgid "`internal-json`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:274
msgid "Outputs the logs in a structured manner."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:278
msgid ""
"While the schema itself is relatively stable, the format of the error-"
"messages (namely of the `msg`\\-field) can change between releases."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:282
msgid "`bar`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:284
msgid "Only display a progress bar during the builds."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:286
msgid "`bar-with-logs`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:288
msgid "Display the raw logs, with the progress bar at the bottom."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:290
msgid ""
"<span id=\"opt-no-build-output\">[`--no-build-output`](#opt-no-build-"
"output)</span> / `-Q`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:292
msgid ""
"By default, output written by builders to standard output and standard error "
"is echoed to the Nix command's standard error. This option suppresses this "
"behaviour. Note that the builder's standard output and error are always "
"written to a log file in `prefix/nix/var/log/nix`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:296
msgid ""
"<span id=\"opt-max-jobs\">[`--max-jobs`](#opt-max-jobs)</span> / `-j` "
"_number_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:298
msgid ""
"Sets the maximum number of build jobs that Nix will perform in parallel to "
"the specified number. Specify `auto` to use the number of CPUs in the "
"system. The default is specified by the `max-jobs` configuration setting, "
"which itself defaults to `1`. A higher value is useful on SMP systems or to "
"exploit I/O latency."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:303
msgid ""
"Setting it to `0` disallows building on the local machine, which is useful "
"when you want builds to happen only on remote builders."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:305
msgid "<span id=\"opt-cores\">[`--cores`](#opt-cores)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:307
msgid ""
"Sets the value of the `NIX_BUILD_CORES` environment variable in the "
"invocation of builders. Builders can use this variable at their discretion "
"to control the maximum amount of parallelism. For instance, in Nixpkgs, if "
"the derivation attribute `enableParallelBuilding` is set to `true`, the "
"builder passes the `-jN` flag to GNU Make. It defaults to the value of the "
"`cores` configuration setting, if set, or `1` otherwise. The value `0` means "
"that the builder should use all available CPU cores in the system."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:313
msgid ""
"<span id=\"opt-max-silent-time\">[`--max-silent-time`](#opt-max-silent-"
"time)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:315
msgid ""
"Sets the maximum number of seconds that a builder can go without producing "
"any data on standard output or standard error. The default is specified by "
"the `max-silent-time` configuration setting. `0` means no time-out."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:319
msgid "<span id=\"opt-timeout\">[`--timeout`](#opt-timeout)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:321
msgid ""
"Sets the maximum number of seconds that a builder can run. The default is "
"specified by the `timeout` configuration setting. `0` means no timeout."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:325
msgid ""
"<span id=\"opt-keep-going\">[`--keep-going`](#opt-keep-going)</span> / `-k`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:327
msgid ""
"Keep going in case of failed builds, to the greatest extent possible. That "
"is, if building an input of some derivation fails, Nix will still build the "
"other inputs, but not the derivation itself. Without this option, Nix stops "
"if any build fails (except for builds of substitutes), possibly killing "
"builds in progress (in case of parallel or distributed builds)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:331
msgid ""
"<span id=\"opt-keep-failed\">[`--keep-failed`](#opt-keep-failed)</span> / `-"
"K`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:333
msgid ""
"Specifies that in case of a build failure, the temporary directory (usually "
"in `/tmp`) in which the build takes place should not be deleted. The path of "
"the build directory is printed as an informational message."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:336
msgid "<span id=\"opt-fallback\">[`--fallback`](#opt-fallback)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:338
msgid ""
"Whenever Nix attempts to build a derivation for which substitutes are known "
"for each output path, but realising the output paths through the substitutes "
"fails, fall back on building the derivation."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:340
msgid ""
"The most common scenario in which this is useful is when we have registered "
"substitutes in order to perform binary distribution from, say, a network "
"repository. If the repository is down, the realisation of the derivation "
"will fail. When this option is specified, Nix will build the derivation "
"instead. Thus, installation from binaries falls back on installation from "
"source. This option is not the default since it is generally not desirable "
"for a transient failure in obtaining the substitutes to lead to a full build "
"from source (with the related consumption of resources)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:346
msgid ""
"<span id=\"opt-readonly-mode\">[`--readonly-mode`](#opt-readonly-mode)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:348
msgid ""
"When this option is used, no attempt is made to open the Nix database. Most "
"Nix operations do need database access, so those operations will fail."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:351
msgid "<span id=\"opt-arg\">[`--arg`](#opt-arg)</span> _name_ _value_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:353
msgid ""
"This option is accepted by `nix-env`, `nix-instantiate`, `nix-shell` and "
"`nix-build`. When evaluating Nix expressions, the expression evaluator will "
"automatically try to call functions that it encounters. It can automatically "
"call functions for which every argument has a [default value](../../language/"
"syntax.md#functions) (e.g., `{ argName ?  defaultValue }: ...`)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:357
msgid ""
"With `--arg`, you can also call functions that have arguments without a "
"default value (or override a default value). That is, if the evaluator "
"encounters a function with an argument named _name_, it will call it with "
"value _value_."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:360
msgid ""
"For instance, the top-level `default.nix` in Nixpkgs is actually a function:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:369
msgid ""
"So if you call this Nix expression (e.g., when you do `nix-env --install --"
"attr pkgname`), the function will be called automatically using the value "
"[`builtins.currentSystem`](../../language/builtins.md) for the `system` "
"argument. You can override this using `--arg`, e.g., `nix-env --install --"
"attr pkgname --arg system \\\"i686-freebsd\\\"`. (Note that since the "
"argument is a Nix string literal, you have to escape the quotes.)"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:373
msgid ""
"<span id=\"opt-arg-from-file\">[`--arg-from-file`](#opt-arg-from-file)</"
"span> _name_ _path_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:375
msgid ""
"Pass the contents of file _path_ as the argument _name_ to Nix functions."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:377
msgid ""
"<span id=\"opt-arg-from-stdin\">[`--arg-from-stdin`](#opt-arg-from-stdin)</"
"span> _name_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:379
msgid "Pass the contents of stdin as the argument _name_ to Nix functions."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:381
msgid "<span id=\"opt-argstr\">[`--argstr`](#opt-argstr)</span> _name_ _value_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:383
msgid ""
"This option is like `--arg`, only the value is not a Nix expression but a "
"string. So instead of `--arg system \\\"i686-linux\\\"` (the outer quotes "
"are to keep the shell happy) you can say `--argstr system i686-linux`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:386
msgid "<span id=\"opt-attr\">[`--attr`](#opt-attr)</span> / `-A` _attrPath_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:388
msgid ""
"Select an attribute from the top-level Nix expression being evaluated. (`nix-"
"env`, `nix-instantiate`, `nix-build` and `nix-shell` only.) The _attribute "
"path_ _attrPath_ is a sequence of attribute names separated by dots. For "
"instance, given a top-level Nix expression _e_, the attribute path `xorg."
"xorgserver` would cause the expression `e.xorg.xorgserver` to be used. See "
"[`nix-env --install`](../../command-ref/nix-env/install.md) for some "
"concrete examples."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:394
msgid ""
"In addition to attribute names, you can also specify array indices. For "
"instance, the attribute path `foo.3.bar` selects the `bar` attribute of the "
"fourth element of the array in the `foo` attribute of the top-level "
"expression."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:399
msgid ""
"<span id=\"opt-eval-store\">[`--eval-store`](#opt-eval-store)</span> _store-"
"url_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:401
msgid ""
"The [URL to the Nix store](../../store/types/index.md#store-url-format) to "
"use for evaluation, i.e. where to store derivations (`.drv` files) and "
"inputs referenced by them."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:403
msgid "<span id=\"opt-expr\">[`--expr`](#opt-expr)</span> / `-E`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:405
msgid ""
"Interpret the command line arguments as a list of Nix expressions to be "
"parsed and evaluated, rather than as a list of file names of Nix "
"expressions. (`nix-instantiate`, `nix-build` and `nix-shell` only.)"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:408
msgid ""
"For `nix-shell`, this option is commonly used to give you a shell in which "
"you can build the packages returned by the expression. If you want to get a "
"shell which contain the _built_ packages ready for use, give your expression "
"to the `nix-shell --packages ` convenience flag instead."
msgstr ""

